WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.486
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.530
Welcome to the MIT Center for
Art, Science, and Technology's

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.880
2021 Symposium, Unfolding
Intelligence, The Art

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.620
and Science of
Contemporary Computation.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.200
CAST was established
in 2012 with the goal

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.750
of building and
building on connections

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.420
between the worlds of art,
science, and technology.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.490
This is the third in
a series of symposia

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.110
that CAST has
convened since then.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:21.170
And as with its predecessors,
we bring together

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:25.610
artists, scientists, engineers,
and humanists from within MIT

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.920
and from the world
at large to discuss

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.900
areas of rapidly
evolving research

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.740
and urgent social relevance
and to find in that dialogue

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:37.740
stimulation, confirmation,
provocation, intersection,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.630
and, we hope, common purpose.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:44.960
At MIT, CAST partners with
departments, labs, and centers

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.360
to integrate the arts
across the curriculum,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.180
to enrich and encourage
artistic collaboration,

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:52.460
and to provide support
to faculty and members

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.740
at the MIT community
as they pursue

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:59.160
their own artistic
practice and/or research.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.250
In addition to
symposia like this,

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.800
CAST facilitates the sharing
of this creative work

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.290
beyond the Institute
by producing concerts,

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:08.900
exhibitions, and
publications and making

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.580
them available to the public.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.220
So thank you for
being with us today.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.220
We hope you will join
us throughout the week

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.610
at virtual events addressing
the aesthetic, technical,

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.910
and critical issues pertaining
to artificial intelligence

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.280
and computational media.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.940
We also look forward to
seeing you on Friday, April 9,

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.750
as the symposium culminates
with a live interactive event

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.440
to which all attendees are
invited in which you can join

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.810
presenters and artists
in breakout rooms

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:41.120
to explore hidden
threads between all that

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.231
has been discussed this week.

00:02:43.231 --> 00:02:46.177
